x86_64-linux  T's constructors and destructor are written inside the class and are inline by nature, so clang emits C2/D2 only and cxx1 emits both of Itanium's forms - see docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol". The names this case exists to check - `pass` and `deref` and their return paths - agree; arm64-darwin agrees on every name and so does x86_64-windows
